This package builds on ArkLib (https://github.com/Verified-zkEVM/ArkLib),
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  - upstream ArkLib main at c488a3a4dabd74c543ee39836523b116dbc7ba2b (2026-11-01),
    fetched from GitHub and pinned in lakefile.toml and lake-manifest.json;
  - plus ten modules of upstream pull requests #1280 (head 3444c2f7) and #1282
    (head 89433a85), both by Quang Dao, which this package imports. Both pull
    requests were closed on GitHub without being merged. The ten files are
    included unchanged except that their module names are moved from ArkLib.* to
    ArkLibFs.* (file paths and the import lines among them; declaration names and
    proofs unchanged; each file carries a modification notice), with their own
    Apache-2.0 headers and ArkLib's LICENSE,
    in vendor/arklib-fs/ (a small Lake package that requires ArkLib at the
    revision above). There is no other ArkLib-side change.

ArkLib's work, used and not re-proved here:
  - Reed-Solomon codes, FRI and batched-FRI soundness, round-by-round and
    state-restoration security (upstream main);
  - the single-salt Fiat-Shamir framework and its security
    (pull requests #1280 and #1282).

This package's own work:
  - NockvmE2E/FriPort: the single-salt Fiat-Shamir soundness of the batched FRI
    used here (batchedFri_singleSalt_soundness), obtained by lifting ArkLib's
    FRI soundness through ArkLib's single-salt framework;
  - NockvmE2E/Lift: the lift from round-by-round soundness to the Fiat-Shamir
    transform for the composed protocol;
  - NockvmE2E/Deep, NockvmE2E/Rap, NockvmE2E/Merkle, NockvmE2E/Succ and the
    end-to-end theorems built on them.

Other Lean dependencies (Mathlib, Batteries, Aesop, VCVio, CompPoly and others)
are used at the revisions in lake-manifest.json, under their own licences.
